{
  "version": "3",
  "notes": [
    "Dividend calendar for backtest trade marking (T2-22, ADR-025). No cash flow and no tax are modelled: a trade is only marked dividend_affected.",
    "Version 3 covers all 20 tickers of config/portfolio.json (T2-22a). The raw API reply is 160 events; scripts/fetch_dividends.py merges payouts that share one ex-date into one payment day, which gives 154 events. Six pairs were merged and each was checked against an independent source (issuer site, T-Invest, RBC, Interfax): CHMF 2020-06-15 27.35+26.26, CHMF 2021-05-31 46.77+36.27, CHMF 2024-06-17 191.51+38.30, LKOH 2022-12-20 537.0+256.0, MAGN 2021-06-16 1.795+0.945, PIKK 2021-05-14 22.92+22.51. They are two payouts with the same record date, not duplicates, so `dividend_gross` is the sum and `payouts` keeps the split.",
    "dividend_gross is the amount per share. The T-Invest field `dividend_net` returns the announced (gross) value: SBER 2024 came back as 33.30 for a declared 33.30 RUB dividend. The API name is misleading, so the field is stored as gross.",
    "last_buy_date is the API's last cum-dividend day. Its meaning changed with the MOEX switch to T+1 on 2023-07-31: before that date the drop sits on the session of last_buy_date, after it on the next session. src/backtest/dividends.py resolves the ex-bar from this date.",
    "source: api - fetched by scripts/fetch_dividends.py; manual - typed by hand and then `reference` is mandatory (independent source, no guessing).",
    "`annotations` is the hand-written layer keyed by TICKER|last_buy_date (status, note, reference). scripts/fetch_dividends.py preserves it on every rewrite, so a re-fetch never loses a checked status.",
    "status: active - paid; not_paid - declared but rejected by the shareholders' meeting (GAZP 2022-10-10, 51.03 RUB, voted down on 2022-09-30). A not_paid event never marks a trade.",
    "Future events (ex-date after the last candle) and events before the first candle stay in the file: the first matter for live shorts, the second are excluded from coverage. Both statuses are computed from the candles, never stored, so they cannot go stale.",
    "An event whose ex-bar does not drop by at least dividends.gap_match_ratio of the expected dividend gap is reported as no_gap_match and is not applied.",
    "Absent events are not invented: the report lists tickers and years the API returned nothing for as unconfirmed, not as 'no dividends', and lists gaps above the threshold that the calendar cannot explain."
  ],
  "annotations": {
    "GAZP|2022-10-10": {
      "status": "not_paid",
      "note": "Interim dividend for H1 2022 of 51.03 RUB per share was recommended by the board but the extraordinary meeting on 2022-09-30 voted it down; the price never dropped by the dividend.",
      "reference": "company disclosure 2022-09-30 (meeting results); Interfax 2022-09-30"
    }
  },
